# VerticalBarChart

## Overview

A complete vertical bar chart component that composes `ChartHeader`, `ChartLegend`, `DataDisplay`, `VerticalBarGroup`, and `ChartFooter` into a cohesive data visualization. `VerticalBarChart` itself is a thin composition/orchestration layer — it has no D3 usage and no runtime JS token resolver; layout math (D3 scales) lives in `VerticalBarGroup`, and all styling reads CSS custom properties directly via `var(--Token-Name)`.

**This component follows the Organized Props Pattern** — top-level booleans (`chartHeader`, `chartLegend`, `dataDisplay`, `chartFooter`) toggle each optional child slot on/off, and a matching `*Config` object (`chartHeaderConfig`, `chartLegendConfig`, `dataDisplayConfig`, `barGroupConfig`, `chartFooterConfig`) configures its contents.

## Figma Reference

- **Node ID**: `41:1436`
- **Design File**: DataVis-Components
- **Figma URL**: https://www.figma.com/design/uA5ExvS0cNXbDEKzT9Rnrt/DataVis-Components?node-id=41-1436

## Architecture

```
VerticalBarChart (flex container, vertical layout)
├── ChartHeader (conditional, when chartHeader=true)
│   ├── ChartTitle
│   └── ChartSubtitle
├── ChartLegend (conditional, when chartLegend=true)
│   └── ChartKey[] (auto-generated or manual)
│       ├── Indicator (circle, line, or dashed)
│       └── Label + optional DataHead
├── DataDisplay (conditional, when dataDisplay=true)
│   ├── contentLeft
│   │   ├── mainLabel (inline typography + optional InfoIcon)
│   │   └── DataHead (DataLead + SupportingData + SupportingLabel)
│   └── contentRight (Badge, from @oneui/ui)
├── VerticalBarGroup (flex-grow)
│   ├── YAxis (optional, when yAxis=true)
│   │   └── ChartAxisTick (for each tick value)
│   └── contentWrapper (flex, space-between)
│       ├── VerticalBar[] (D3-scaled heights, for visible data)
│       │   ├── hitArea (transparent overlay, extends to next bar)
│       │   ├── topLabel (inline typography tokens)
│       │   ├── ShapeRect (bar, pointer-events: none when hitArea active)
│       │   └── categoryLabel (inline typography tokens)
│       └── VerticalStackedBar (conditional, for "Others" overflow group)
│           ├── hitArea (transparent overlay, hover → first segment data)
│           ├── topLabel (inline typography — accumulated sum)
│           ├── stackedBars (segment per overflow item, sequential colors, z-index: 2)
│           │   └── segment[] (flex-grow proportional to value)
│           └── categoryLabel (inline typography — "Others")
└── ChartFooter (conditional, when chartFooter=true)
    ├── annotationLeft (inline typography tokens)
    └── annotationRight (inline typography tokens)
```

## Canonical Default Render

> **This is what consumers should get when they request a `VerticalBarChart` without supplying extra detail.** It is the spec: the `Default` story in `VerticalBarChart.stories.tsx` matches this exactly, and any future change to the canonical baseline must update the story, this section, and the meta `docs.description` together.

### What's ON by default

| Part                            | Default                 | Why                                                                                                                      |
| ------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `ChartHeader`                   | **ON**                  | Title + subtitle anchor the chart so the reader knows what they're looking at                                            |
| `barGroupConfig.categoryLabels` | **ON**                  | The X-axis identifies each bar                                                                                           |
| `barGroupConfig.hoverBadge`     | **ON**                  | Cursor-following `DataBadge` for per-bar value reveal — the cheapest way to surface exact values without `topDataLabels` |
| `ChartFooter`                   | **ON**                  | Slot for source / footnote annotations                                                                                   |
| `interactive`                   | **ON** (default `true`) | Bars receive hover / click / focus handlers                                                                              |
| `barGroupConfig.barWidth`       | **`"M"`**               | Default bar width                                                                                                        |

### What's OFF by default (opt-in only)

| Part                                      | When to enable                                                                                                                       |
| ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `chartLegend`                             | When the chart needs a legend chip (e.g. summary value via `chartLegendConfig.dataHead`); single-series charts often skip it         |
| `dataDisplay`                             | Only when paired with a primary KPI / summary surface that benefits from a static or hover-driven `DataDisplay` block above the bars |
| `barGroupConfig.yAxis`                    | Quantitative reference gridlines — turn on when relative magnitude matters more than the per-bar value                               |
| `barGroupConfig.topDataLabels`            | Show the exact value above each bar (alternative to `hoverBadge` for static, non-interactive consumers)                              |
| `barGroupConfig.avgLine`                  | Comparison against the dataset mean / a fixed threshold                                                                              |
| `animated`                                | Datasets that change at runtime (filters, scenario toggles)                                                                          |
| `valueFormat` / `barGroupConfig.dataSort` | Domain-specific formatting / sorting needs                                                                                           |
| `categoryLabelConfig` overrides           | Long category names that need word / line-clamp tuning, or `overflowType: "grouped"` for an "Others" bundle                          |
| `accessibility.enabled`                   | Production charts (always opt in for shipped charts; off in this default for the rendered Storybook demo)                            |

### Minimal canonical example

```tsx
<VerticalBarChart
  data={canonicalData}
  chartHeader
  chartFooter
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: "Monthly Revenue",
    chartSubtitleValue: "Q1-Q2 2024 Performance Overview",
  }}
  barGroupConfig={{
    categoryLabels: true,
    barWidth: "M",
    hoverBadge: true,
  }}
  chartFooterConfig={{
    annotationLeftValue: "Source: Internal Analytics",
    annotationRightValue: "*In thousands USD",
  }}
/>
```

> **Authoring rule:** when a consumer (human or LLM) asks for "a VerticalBarChart" without further detail, render the example above — _not_ the `Anatomy` story (everything turned on at once). Anatomy exists as a reference; the default is what ships in real product surfaces.

## Import

```tsx
import { VerticalBarChart } from "@oneui/datavis/components/charts/VerticalBarChart";
// or from the barrel:
import { VerticalBarChart } from "@oneui/datavis";
```

## Data Formats

### ChartDataPoint (Canonical - Recommended)

```tsx
import { ChartDataPoint } from "@oneui/datavis/types/chart-data";

interface ChartDataPoint {
  id?: string; // Unique identifier for React keys
  category: CategoryValue; // Category label (e.g., "Jan")
  value: number; // Numeric value for bar height
  color?: string; // Optional custom color for the bar
  colorIndex?: number; // Categorical color index (1-6)
}
```

### DataPoint (Legacy - Deprecated)

```tsx
/**
 * @deprecated Use ChartDataPoint from '../types/chart-data' instead.
 */
interface DataPoint {
  label: string; // Category label (e.g., "Jan")
  value: number; // Numeric value for bar height
  color?: string; // Optional custom color for the bar
}
```

> **Migration Note**: See `docs/DATA-FORMAT.md` for full specification and migration guide.

## Props Interface (Organized Props Pattern)

```tsx
import { DataPoint } from "../../groups/VerticalBarGroup";
import { ChartDataPoint } from "../../../types/chart-data";
import { ChartLegendItem } from "../../groups/ChartLegend";

/** Props for the ChartHeader child component */
type ChartHeaderConfig = Pick<
  ChartHeaderProps,
  "chartTitleValue" | "chartSubtitleValue" | "title" | "subtitle" | "titleId" | "subtitleId"
>;

/** Props for the ChartLegend child component */
interface ChartLegendConfig {
  items?: ChartLegendItem[];
  categoryLabelValue?: string;
  type?: "circle" | "dashed" | "line";
  dataHead?: boolean;
  dataHeadConfig?: {
    dataLeadValue?: number | string;
    dataSupportingValue?: number | string;
    supportingLabelValue?: string;
    supportingData?: boolean;
    supportingLabel?: boolean;
  };
  /** Typography size variant. Controls legend item scaling. */
  size?: "XS" | "S" | "M" | "L" | "XL";
  /** Forwarded to ChartLegend's aria-label. */
  ariaLabel?: string;
  /** Forwarded to ChartLegend's aria-labelledby; takes precedence over ariaLabel when set. */
  ariaLabelledBy?: string;
}

/** Hover event data passed to callbacks */
export type { VerticalBarHoverData } from "../../groups/VerticalBarGroup";

/** Category label display rules */
interface CategoryLabelConfig {
  maxWords?: number; // Max words per label (default: 3)
  maxLines?: number; // Max display lines (default: 1)
  othersLabel?: string; // Label for overflow group (default: "Others")
  /** @deprecated Use overflowType instead */
  /** @deprecated Use overflowType instead */
  enableOverflowGrouping?: boolean; // Group overflow into "Others" (default: false)
  overflowType?: "grouped" | "truncated" | "all"; // Overflow strategy (default: "truncated")
  skippedLabels?: "auto" | number; // Label skip mode for overflowType "all" (default: "auto")
}

/** Y-axis configuration */
interface YAxisConfig {
  tickCount?: number;
  formatValue?: (value: number) => string;
}

/** Average line configuration */
interface AvgLineConfig {
  formatValue?: (value: number) => string;
  type?: "avg" | "threshold";
  thresholdValue?: number;
}

/** Hover badge configuration */
interface HoverBadgeConfig {
  formatValue?: (value: number, label?: string) => string;
  formatBadge?: (data: VerticalBarHoverData) => DataBadgeConfig;
}

/** Props for the VerticalBarGroup child component */
interface BarGroupConfig {
  topDataLabels?: boolean;
  categoryLabels?: boolean;
  yAxis?: boolean;
  avgLine?: boolean;
  hoverBadge?: boolean;
  valueFormat?: ValueFormatConfig;
  barWidth?: string;
  /** Callback fired when any bar hover state changes */
  onBarHover?: (data: VerticalBarHoverData) => void;
  /** Callback fired when any bar is clicked */
  onBarClick?: (data: VerticalBarHoverData) => void;
  /**
   * Back-compat alias for `highlightedBarIndices`. Accepts a single index
   * (`number`) or an array (`number[]`). New code should prefer
   * `highlightedBarIndices`.
   */
  hoveredBarIndex?: number | number[];
  /**
   * Indices of bars rendered at full opacity; every other bar dims.
   * Use to programmatically highlight one or more bars (e.g. syncing
   * selection across multiple charts or with an external data table).
   * Takes precedence over `hoveredBarIndex` when both are supplied.
   */
  highlightedBarIndices?: number[];
  /** Y-axis display configuration */
  yAxisConfig?: YAxisConfig;
  /** Average line display configuration */
  avgLineConfig?: AvgLineConfig;
  /** Hover badge display configuration */
  hoverBadgeConfig?: HoverBadgeConfig;
  /** Category label display rules */
  categoryLabelConfig?: CategoryLabelConfig;
  /** Sort bars by value: "asc" | "desc" | "unsorted" (default: "unsorted") */
  dataSort?: DataSortOrder;
}

/** Props for the ChartFooter child component */
type ChartFooterConfig = Pick<
  ChartFooterProps,
  "annotationLeft" | "annotationLeftValue" | "annotationRight" | "annotationRightValue"
>;

/**
 * Props for the DataDisplay child component.
 * Mirrors DataDisplayProps structure (Layer 2 + Layer 3), with additional
 * chart-specific props for hover behaviour.
 * When mode is "hover", mainLabelValue, dataHead.dataLeadValue, and
 * badgeConfig.value update dynamically on hover.
 */
interface DataDisplayConfig {
  // --- Chart-specific behaviour ---
  /** Display mode: "static" uses provided values, "hover" updates dynamically on hover (default: "static") */
  mode?: "static" | "hover";
  /** Custom formatter for lead value in hover mode */
  formatHoverLeadValue?: (value: number, category?: CategoryValue) => string;
  /** Custom formatter for badge value in hover mode */
  formatHoverBadgeValue?: (value: number, category?: CategoryValue) => string;

  // --- DataDisplay Layer 2 props ---
  /** The main label text above the data value */
  mainLabelValue?: string;
  /** Layout alignment: "Left" (horizontal) or "Center" (vertical stacked) (default: "Left") */
  alignment?: "Left" | "Center";
  /** Toggle visibility of the rightBadgeWrapper section (default: true) */
  rightBadgeWrapper?: boolean;
  /** Toggle visibility of the badgeTop slot (default: false) */
  badgeTop?: boolean;
  /** Toggle visibility of the badgeBottom slot (default: true) */
  badgeBottom?: boolean;
  /** Toggle visibility of the OneUI Badge in supporting slots (default: true) */
  showBadge?: boolean;
  /** Toggle visibility of the supporting label next to the badge (default: true) */
  supportingBadgeLabel?: boolean;
  /** The supporting label text next to the badge */
  supportingBadgeLabelValue?: string;
  /** Local size variant for typography scaling: "XS", "S", "M", "L", or "XL" (default: "L") */
  size?: "XS" | "S" | "M" | "L" | "XL";

  // --- DataDisplay Layer 3 configs ---
  /** Configuration for the DataHead child component */
  dataHead?: DataHeadConfig;
  /** Configuration for the Badge + SupportingLabel in supporting slots */
  badgeConfig?: BadgeConfig;
}

interface VerticalBarChartProps {
  // Layer 2: Parent component props
  /**
   * Supports both canonical format (ChartDataPoint[]) and legacy format (DataPoint[]).
   * Canonical format (recommended): { category, value, color?, colorIndex? }
   * Legacy format (deprecated): { label, value, color?, colorIndex? }
   */
  data: ChartDataPoint[] | DataPoint[];
  width?: number | string;
  height?: number | string;
  /** Stretch chart to fill its parent container width (default: false) */
  fullWidth?: boolean;
  chartHeader?: boolean;
  chartFooter?: boolean;
  chartLegend?: boolean;
  /** Whether to show the DataDisplay component above the bar group */
  dataDisplay?: boolean;
  /** Enable hover/click interactivity on bars (default: true) */
  interactive?: boolean;
  /** Enable entry animation where bars grow from bottom to top on first load (default: false) */
  animated?: boolean;

  // Layer 3: Child component configurations
  chartHeaderConfig?: ChartHeaderConfig;
  chartLegendConfig?: ChartLegendConfig;
  /** Configuration for DataDisplay: { mode, label, leadValue, badgeValue, ... } */
  dataDisplayConfig?: DataDisplayConfig;
  barGroupConfig?: BarGroupConfig;
  chartFooterConfig?: ChartFooterConfig;

  // Accessibility
  accessibility?: AccessibilityConfig;
}
```

## Props

### Parent Component Props (Layer 2)

| Prop          | Type                              | Default | Description                                                                          |
| ------------- | --------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `data`        | `ChartDataPoint[] \| DataPoint[]` | `[]`    | Array of data points (canonical or legacy)                                           |
| `width`       | `number \| string`                | `328`   | Total width of the chart                                                             |
| `height`      | `number \| string`                | `400`   | **Total height of the chart.** VerticalBarGroup automatically fills remaining space. |
| `fullWidth`   | `boolean`                         | `false` | Stretch chart to fill its parent container width                                     |
| `chartHeader` | `boolean`                         | `true`  | Show/hide the chart header                                                           |
| `chartFooter` | `boolean`                         | `true`  | Show/hide the chart footer                                                           |
| `chartLegend` | `boolean`                         | `false` | Show/hide the chart legend                                                           |
| `dataDisplay` | `boolean`                         | `false` | Show/hide DataDisplay component above the bar group                                  |
| `interactive` | `boolean`                         | `true`  | Enable hover/click interactivity on bars                                             |
| `animated`    | `boolean`                         | `false` | Enable entry animation where bars grow from bottom to top on first load              |

### ChartHeader Config (`chartHeaderConfig`)

| Prop                 | Type     | Default     | Description         |
| -------------------- | -------- | ----------- | ------------------- |
| `chartTitleValue`    | `string`  | `"This is chart title."` | Chart title text    |
| `chartSubtitleValue` | `string`  | `"This is chart subtitle supporting the title and providing additional context."` | Chart subtitle text |
| `title`              | `boolean` | `true`      | Show the title element |
| `subtitle`           | `boolean` | `true`      | Show the subtitle element |
| `titleId`            | `string`  | `undefined` | `id` applied to the title element; lets a consumer point their own `aria-labelledby` at it |
| `subtitleId`         | `string`  | `undefined` | `id` applied to the subtitle element; lets a consumer point their own `aria-describedby` at it |

