### Overflow Type: Truncated (Hide Non-Fitting Bars)

With `overflowType: "truncated"`, no "Others" bar is created. In **fluid** mode, bars that don't fit are trimmed from the right to prevent label overlap. In **fixed** mode, all bars are shown as-is.

```tsx
// Fluid mode (default): bars trimmed from the right when they don't fit
<VerticalBarChart
  data={manyCategories}
  barGroupConfig={{
    categoryLabelConfig: {
      overflowType: "truncated",
      labelWidth: "fluid",
    },
  }}
/>

// Fixed mode: all bars shown regardless of fit
<VerticalBarChart
  data={manyCategories}
  barGroupConfig={{
    categoryLabelConfig: {
      overflowType: "truncated",
      labelWidth: 80,
    },
  }}
/>
```

### Overflow Type: All (Show All Bars, Skip Labels)

With `overflowType: "all"`, every bar in the dataset is rendered but in-between category labels are dynamically hidden to prevent overlapping. This is ideal for dense sequential data like years or months where showing all bars matters but not every label is needed.

Hovering any bar — including those with hidden labels — reveals the full category name in the hover badge and the `onBarHover` callback. This ensures users can always discover which category a bar belongs to.

```tsx
// Auto mode (default): dynamically determines which labels to show
<VerticalBarChart
  data={yearlyData} // e.g., 20 years of data
  barGroupConfig={{
    categoryLabels: true,
    hoverBadge: true,
    categoryLabelConfig: {
      overflowType: "all",
    },
  }}
/>

// Explicit skip interval: show every other label (skip 1 in between)
<VerticalBarChart
  data={yearlyData}
  barGroupConfig={{
    categoryLabels: true,
    categoryLabelConfig: {
      overflowType: "all",
      skippedLabels: 1, // show every 2nd label
    },
  }}
/>

// Show every 3rd label (skip 2 in between)
<VerticalBarChart
  data={yearlyData}
  barGroupConfig={{
    categoryLabels: true,
    categoryLabelConfig: {
      overflowType: "all",
      skippedLabels: 2,
    },
  }}
/>
```

