## Hover Badge

The VerticalBarChart supports a cursor-following DataBadge that displays the value of the hovered bar.

### Enabling Hover Badge

```tsx
<VerticalBarChart
  data={data}
  interactive={true} // Required for hover badge
  barGroupConfig={{
    hoverBadge: true,
  }}
/>
```

### Custom Value Formatting

```tsx
// Using hoverBadgeConfig.formatValue for custom format
<VerticalBarChart
  data={data}
  barGroupConfig={{
    hoverBadge: true,
    hoverBadgeConfig: {
      formatValue: (value, label) => `${label}: £${value.toLocaleString()}`,
    },
  }}
/>

// Using valueFormat (applies to all chart values)
<VerticalBarChart
  data={data}
  barGroupConfig={{
    hoverBadge: true,
    valueFormat: { type: "currency", currency: "GBP" },
  }}
/>
```

### How It Works

`hoverBadge` and `hoverBadgeConfig` are forwarded as-is to `VerticalBarGroup` (which owns the actual hover badge implementation — see [VerticalBarGroup.md](../../groups/VerticalBarGroup/VerticalBarGroup.md#hover-badge) for the full mechanism). Summary:

1. **Requires `interactive={true}`**: The hover badge only appears when interactivity is enabled (default)
2. **Smart positioning**: The badge flips into the nearest quadrant based on cursor position within the container
3. **Always visible**: This ensures the badge doesn't get cut off at the edges, even with long text values
4. **Value formatting**: Uses `hoverBadgeConfig.formatValue` if provided, otherwise falls back to `valueFormat` or raw value

## DataDisplay Integration

This chart supports an optional DataDisplay component positioned between ChartLegend and the group component — see the "DataDisplay Config" props tables above and the "With DataDisplay" usage examples for static/hover modes, custom formatters, and requirements.

## Accessibility

Wrapped by `ChartAccessibility` (enabled by default). This chart has **full accessibility wiring**, including:

| Feature               | Implementation                                                                                                                                                   |
| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **ARIA wrapper**      | `role="figure"`, `aria-label`, `aria-describedby` with auto summary + data table                                                                                 |
| **ARIA live region**  | `aria-live="polite"` announces `"{category}, {value}, {pct}% of total"` on hover/focus via `useChartAccessibility` (which debounces through `useAriaLiveRegion`) |
| **Roving tabindex**   | Single tab stop — Arrow Left/Right navigates bars, Home/End jump to first/last via `useRovingTabIndex`                                                           |
| **Bar semantics**     | `aria-roledescription="data point"`, positional label embedded in `aria-label` (e.g., "bar 1 of 10")                                                             |
| **Controls linking**  | `aria-controls` on each bar points to DataDisplay (when enabled)                                                                                                 |
| **Decorative hiding** | YAxis, AvgLine, ZeroLine, and the hover badge all `aria-hidden="true"`                                                                                            |
| **Legend structure**  | ChartLegend rendered as `role="list"` with `role="listitem"` entries                                                                                             |

No additional consumer configuration needed — all features activate automatically when `accessibility.enabled` is `true` (the default).

Implemented via the shared `ChartAccessibility` wrapper (`../../ChartAccessibility.tsx`) and the `useChartAccessibility` hook (`../../../hooks/useChartAccessibility.ts`) — the same pattern used by other chart components in this package.

